infographic sequence-ascending-steps
data
  title Connascence strength ladder: weakest to strongest
  desc Management cost rises with strength; the static→dynamic boundary is where the type checker stops catching it
  order asc
  sequences
    - label CoN — Name
      desc Static · share an identifier; a rename fixes it everywhere
    - label CoT — Type
      desc Static · share a type declaration
    - label CoM — Meaning
      desc Static · share a value convention; silent runtime misclassification
    - label CoP — Position
      desc Static · share argument order; reordering compiles yet passes wrong values
    - label CoA — Algorithm
      desc Static · share an implementation; invisible to the type system
    - label CoE — Execution
      desc Dynamic · share a runtime call order
    - label CoV — Values
      desc Dynamic · share runtime data across copies
    - label CoI — Identity
      desc Dynamic · share the same object reference
